DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
1202::$$$message_0006_0000_0000$$$::I'll go hang out in Rider's room.[lr]::
1203::$$$message_0006_0000_0001$$$::She's probably reading a book as always.::
1204::$$$message_0006_0001_0000$$$::"Hey, Rider, ah..."[lr]::
1205::$$$message_0006_0001_0001$$$::"..."::
1206::$$$message_0006_0002_0000$$$::What a great timing.[lr]::
1207::$$$message_0006_0002_0001$$$::Just as I'm about to ask if she's free, she slips by me.::
1208::$$$message_0006_0003_0000$$$::"Huh?"[lr]::
1209::$$$message_0006_0003_0001$$$::She leaves quickly. Maybe she has something urgent to do.[lr]::
1210::$$$message_0006_0003_0002$$$::Oh well. I'll just have tea by myself.::
1211::$$$message_0006_0004_0000$$$::"Yes... I'd like to make an appointment today... No."::
1212::$$$message_0006_0005_0000$$$::...I run into Rider again.[lr]::
1213::$$$message_0006_0005_0001$$$::I'll make enough tea for her, too.[lr]::
1214::$$$message_0006_0005_0002$$$::There's still some water boiling in the pot, so I quickly brew more green tea.::
1215::$$$message_0006_0006_0000$$$::"Are you available in the afternoon?[lr]::
1216::$$$message_0006_0006_0001$$$::The stylist is... Haah, please thank her for her trouble.[lr]::
1217::$$$message_0006_0006_0002$$$::Three o'clock, then. Thank you."::
1218::$$$message_0006_0007_0000$$$::Stylist?[lr]::
1219::$$$message_0006_0007_0001$$$::...I return to the living room with the tea and offer it to Rider.::
1220::$$$message_0006_0008_0000$$$::"Calling somewhere, Rider?"[lr]::
1221::$$$message_0006_0008_0001$$$::"Yes. I called the beauty salon."::
1222::$$$message_0006_0009_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
1223::$$$message_0006_0009_0001$$$::I'm not exactly sure why I'm surprised, but it's like something just bonked me on the head.[lr]::
1224::$$$message_0006_0009_0002$$$::...Right, Rider's a grown woman. It makes sense she'd go to a salon... But would someone this beautiful go to a beauty salon in Miyama that high school students use?::
1225::$$$message_0006_0010_0000$$$::"You mean the salon in Miyama?"[lr]::
1226::$$$message_0006_0010_0001$$$::"Yes. It's difficult for me to tend to this much hair on my own.[lr]::
1227::$$$message_0006_0010_0002$$$::I take the time to visit roughly twice a week to get my hair treated."::
1228::$$$message_0006_0011_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
1229::$$$message_0006_0011_0001$$$::Rider's hair, huh.[lr]::
1230::$$$message_0006_0011_0002$$$::Now that I look at it, it looks like it's very silky and would feel good enough to make one want to touch it.[lr]::
1231::$$$message_0006_0011_0003$$$::...Should I? I'd like to play with it just once... No, control yourself, man. That would be risking my own life.::
1232::$$$message_0006_0012_0000$$$::"Hm? You have to get your hair cut? Does it get too long?"[lr]::
1233::$$$message_0006_0012_0001$$$::"No, it doesn't grow, but it does get messy... And besides..."::
1234::$$$message_0006_0013_0000$$$::Rider takes a sip of her tea.::
1235::$$$message_0006_0014_0000$$$::"When I change to spirit form and back to material form, my hair goes back to its original state."[lr]::
1236::$$$message_0006_0014_0001$$$::"So why don't you just do that...?"::
1237::$$$message_0006_0015_0000$$$::"I don't want to burden Sakura with something as trivial as my hair.[lr]::
1238::$$$message_0006_0015_0001$$$::...It's really quite troublesome, but I should take care of my hair on my own.[lr]::
1239::$$$message_0006_0015_0002$$$::To be honest, I get into a bad mood when it's messy."::
1240::$$$message_0006_0016_0000$$$::"I see. Women sure have a lot to worry about, huh."[lr]::
1241::$$$message_0006_0016_0001$$$::"I appreciate the thought, Shirou.[lr]::
1242::$$$message_0006_0016_0002$$$::But if you care, then please prioritize Sakura over me. I am merely her Servant."::
1243::$$$message_0006_0017_0000$$$::"Sakura likes it when you care for her.[lr]::
1244::$$$message_0006_0017_0001$$$::And it makes me happy to see you both that way."[lr]::
1245::$$$message_0006_0017_0002$$$::"Hm... O-okay. I'll do my best."::
1246::$$$message_0006_0018_0000$$$::"Yes. For you, it may be harder than fighting, but do make an effort... At the risk of repeating myself, I do enjoy watching you try."[lr]::
1247::$$$message_0006_0018_0001$$$::"Urgh."[lr]::
1248::$$$message_0006_0018_0002$$$::What a scary remark.::
1249::$$$message_0006_0019_0000$$$::"U-um, I care about Sakura plenty.[lr]::
1250::$$$message_0006_0019_0001$$$::What about Tohsaka? I wonder if she goes to the salon too."[lr]::
1251::$$$message_0006_0019_0002$$$::"I think your concerns for her are unnecessary, even unwanted."[lr]::
1252::$$$message_0006_0019_0003$$$::She answers instantly.::
1253::$$$message_0006_0020_0000$$$::"...Lest you misunderstand,[lr]::
1254::$$$message_0006_0020_0001$$$::Rin does not like to show her efforts. I think she would feel ashamed if you find out how much effort she puts into her appearance."[lr]::
1255::$$$message_0006_0020_0002$$$::"Ahh... I see."[lr]::
1256::$$$message_0006_0020_0003$$$::It's like how a swan, with all its elegance, still has to paddle hard beneath the water.[lr]::
1257::$$$message_0006_0020_0004$$$::Thinking of the rest of the girls in my house...::
1258::$$$message_0006_0021_0000$$$::"What about Saber?"[lr]::
1259::$$$message_0006_0021_0001$$$::"It's hard to tell. She becomes belligerent when I suggest she visit the salon, but I think she would take it as an advice if you tell her to."[lr]::
1260::$$$message_0006_0021_0002$$$::[chgfg time=300 storage=ライダー私服01a(中) textoff=0]Yeah, it's hard to predict how that would turn out.[lr]::
1261::$$$message_0006_0021_0003$$$::She would probably say something like...she prefers her current hairstyle, or that other styles wouldn't look good on her.::
1262::$$$message_0006_0022_0000$$$::"And Fuji-nee... I wonder, haha."[lr]::
1263::$$$message_0006_0022_0001$$$::Seriously, who knows?[lr]::
1264::$$$message_0006_0022_0002$$$::"She might be happy."[lr]::
1265::$$$message_0006_0022_0003$$$::"Huh?"::
1266::$$$message_0006_0023_0000$$$::"I said she might be happy.[lr]::
1267::$$$message_0006_0023_0001$$$::She isn't the type to apply cosmetics, but I don't think she dislikes it.[lr]::
1268::$$$message_0006_0023_0002$$$::If you told her you wanted to go to the salon, she'd probably instantly ask to join you."::
1269::$$$message_0006_0024_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
1270::$$$message_0006_0024_0001$$$::Hold on.[lr]::
1271::$$$message_0006_0024_0002$$$::When did this become about me going?::
1272::$$$message_0006_0025_0000$$$::"...Leaving me aside for now...[lr]::
1273::$$$message_0006_0025_0001$$$::Are you going now?"[lr]::
1274::$$$message_0006_0025_0002$$$::"My appointment is in the afternoon. I can relax until then."[lr]::
1275::$$$message_0006_0025_0003$$$::With that, she sits at her usual spot in front of the TV.::
1276::$$$message_0006_0026_0000$$$::"...On that topic, I don't really like going there."[lr]::
1277::$$$message_0006_0026_0001$$$::She murmurs as if to herself.[lr]::
1278::$$$message_0006_0026_0002$$$::"Huh?"[lr]::
1279::$$$message_0006_0026_0003$$$::She doesn't like the beauty salon?::
1280::$$$message_0006_0027_0000$$$::"Why? It sounded like you were used to going."[lr]::
1281::$$$message_0006_0027_0001$$$::"Because...there are mirrors there."[lr]::
1282::$$$message_0006_0027_0002$$$::"Ah."[lr]::
1283::$$$message_0006_0027_0003$$$::Of course that would make sense.[lr]::
1284::$$$message_0006_0027_0004$$$::Rider's True Name is Medusa, and she was defeated due to a mirrored shield.::
1285::$$$message_0006_0028_0000$$$::"...There was a mirrored shield in your legend, right?[lr]::
1286::$$$message_0006_0028_0001$$$::It's said that it reflected your Mystic Eyes of Petrification."[lr]::
1287::$$$message_0006_0028_0002$$$::According to Greek mythology, the hero Perseus used a mirrored shield to suppress the monster Medusa's Mystic Eyes before decapitating her.[lr]::
1288::$$$message_0006_0028_0003$$$::...?[lr]::
1289::$$$message_0006_0028_0004$$$::Wait, but wouldn't that mean...::
1290::$$$message_0006_0029_0000$$$::"Rider, you have to take off your glasses when you get your hair cut, right?[lr]::
1291::$$$message_0006_0029_0001$$$::And if you have to sit in front of a mirror...wouldn't you petrify yourself?"[lr]::
1292::$$$message_0006_0029_0002$$$::"No. I will not be petrified simply by looking into a mirror.[lr]::
1293::$$$message_0006_0029_0003$$$::Perseus used the mirror to fight me without making direct eye contact with me."::
1294::$$$message_0006_0030_0000$$$::"Oh, I see."[lr]::
1295::$$$message_0006_0030_0001$$$::So the mirrored shield didn't reflect her eyes' power.[lr]::
1296::$$$message_0006_0030_0002$$$::Perseus combated the Mystic Eyes by not allowing them to make direct contact with him.::
1297::$$$message_0006_0031_0000$$$::"Hm...? Then what's wrong with mirrors?[lr]::
1298::$$$message_0006_0031_0001$$$::It's not like the mirror killed you, and while I can see why you wouldn't like mirrors, aren't you kind of overreacting?"[lr]::
1299::$$$message_0006_0031_0002$$$::"...Not necessarily.[lr]::
1300::$$$message_0006_0031_0003$$$::Even if the goddess's shield didn't literally seal my eyes, the fact remains that a mirror defeated me."::
1301::$$$message_0006_0032_0000$$$::"Hm?"[lr]::
1302::$$$message_0006_0032_0001$$$::This is a mystery.[lr]::
1303::$$$message_0006_0032_0002$$$::It sounds like there's some truth behind the legendary slaying of Medusa that isn't commonly known.::
1304::$$$message_0006_0033_0000$$$::"...[wvl canskip=0 time=700]Do you want to know, Shirou?"[lr]::
1305::$$$message_0006_0033_0001$$$::"Huh? Uh, well...I am curious."[lr]::
1306::$$$message_0006_0033_0002$$$::"Do you insist on knowing?"[lr]::
1307::$$$message_0006_0033_0003$$$::"Well, I don't [font italic=true]need[font italic=false] to know..."::
1308::$$$message_0006_0034_0000$$$::After all, it would be the story of Medusa[line len=2]I mean, Rider's defeat.[lr]::
1309::$$$message_0006_0034_0001$$$::I'm not going to force her to tell me.[lr]::
1310::$$$message_0006_0034_0002$$$::"...Um.[lr]::
1311::$$$message_0006_0034_0003$$$::I'd like you to tell me about it, if you're willing to."::
1312::$$$message_0006_0035_0000$$$::"Very well.[lr]::
1313::$$$message_0006_0035_0001$$$::I don't like recalling those events, but since you asked, I'll describe them.[lr]::
1314::$$$message_0006_0035_0002$$$::It occurred after I had matured as a monster.[lr]::
1315::$$$message_0006_0035_0003$$$::They were the last days of a monster that had fallen far beyond the person you know now..."::
1316::$$$message_0006_0036_0000$$$::The peaceful noontime feels heavier somehow.[lr]::
1317::$$$message_0006_0036_0001$$$::Rider seems to have something in mind. Or she might be looking forward to my fearful reaction.[lr]::
1318::$$$message_0006_0036_0002$$$::Quietly, she begins to talk about the end of her life.::
1319::$$$message_0006_0037_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"...Ask me for anything else.[font italic=false][lr]::
1320::$$$message_0006_0037_0001$$$::    [font italic=true]I will even bring back the head of the alleged Gorgon, if you demand it."[font italic=false]::
1321::$$$message_0006_0038_0000$$$::Perseus, who would later be known as the king of Tiryns[lr]::
1322::$$$message_0006_0038_0001$$$::and Mycenae, spoke at a feast.[lr]::
1323::$$$message_0006_0038_0002$$$::In the Greek world, he was the hero most beloved by the gods.[lr]::
1324::$$$message_0006_0038_0003$$$::One day, Perseus, son of Zeus, declared war on the monster in order to defend his own valor and mother.::
1325::$$$message_0006_0039_0000$$$::...That lone island was one of the penal colonies for beings exiled from the pantheon of gods.[lr]::
1326::$$$message_0006_0039_0001$$$::A monster lurked at the ends of the sea.[lr]::
1327::$$$message_0006_0039_0002$$$::The stories described it as devilish as a siren, as enormous as a titan, and as chaotic as a chimera.[lr]::
1328::$$$message_0006_0039_0003$$$::Not a shadow of the formerly beautiful temple remained. It had become an incomparably inhuman realm of evil.[lr]::
1329::$$$message_0006_0039_0004$$$::The temple was called the Shapeless Isle.[lr]::
1330::$$$message_0006_0039_0005$$$::Even sea birds would not approach it. It was an underworld protruding onto the surface of the earth.::
1331::$$$message_0006_0040_0000$$$::Perseus was granted five relics: [lr]::
1332::$$$message_0006_0040_0001$$$::winged sandals that allowed their wearer to fly,[lr]::
1333::$$$message_0006_0040_0002$$$::a helmet that rendered its wearer invisible,[lr]::
1334::$$$message_0006_0040_0003$$$::a bronze shield from Athena, polished to a mirror finish,[lr]::
1335::$$$message_0006_0040_0004$$$::the snake-hunting scythe Harpe,[lr]::
1336::$$$message_0006_0040_0005$$$::and according to later legend, Kibisis, a sack to contain the head of the monster.::
1337::$$$message_0006_0041_0000$$$::No hero had ever been granted so many godly relics.[lr]::
1338::$$$message_0006_0041_0001$$$::Perseus was equipped for victory. He also learned much about his target to avoid failure.[lr]::
1339::$$$message_0006_0041_0002$$$::He had reliable arms, and strategies to support them.[lr]::
1340::$$$message_0006_0041_0003$$$::He did not feel a single shred of fear towards his yet-unknown enemy in a yet-unvisited demonic realm.[lr]::
1341::$$$message_0006_0041_0004$$$::On the day of the battle...[lr]::
1342::$$$message_0006_0041_0005$$$::The moment he stepped foot in the dark temple...::
1343::$$$message_0006_0042_0000$$$::...The island was nothing like the rumors.[lr]::
1344::$$$message_0006_0042_0001$$$::Sunlight could not reach it. The air was stagnant. The very realm dissolved organic matter.[lr]::
1345::$$$message_0006_0042_0002$$$::The bloody, dark temple was a hellscape that did not abide life.[lr]::
1346::$$$message_0006_0042_0003$$$::A visitor might wonder if they had died and descended into Hades.[lr]::
1347::$$$message_0006_0042_0004$$$::No matter how blessed he was by the gods, this was not something that Perseus, who had yet to accomplish anything heroic, could face on his own.::
1348::$$$message_0006_0043_0000$$$::Perseus proceeded into the depths of the temple, as if he was chased into it.[lr]::
1349::$$$message_0006_0043_0001$$$::His delusions of grandeur about triumphantly slaying the monster were long gone.[lr]::
1350::$$$message_0006_0043_0002$$$::He no longer craved glory.[lr]::
1351::$$$message_0006_0043_0003$$$::His only wish was to find the monster as soon as possible, sever its head as soon as possible, and get off this island as soon as possible.::
1352::$$$message_0006_0044_0000$$$::The burning air roasted his flesh, and the earth slowly melted his feet.[lr]::
1353::$$$message_0006_0044_0001$$$::His defeat was assured if he stayed overlong.[lr]::
1354::$$$message_0006_0044_0002$$$::The reckless challenger would die before he ever reached the monster slumbering in the temple depths.::
1355::$$$message_0006_0045_0000$$$::Perseus held his breath, silenced his steps, choked down his screams, and crept into the temple, darting from shadow to shadow.[lr]::
1356::$$$message_0006_0045_0001$$$::The temple was vast.[lr]::
1357::$$$message_0006_0045_0002$$$::Not just large, but excessively expansive.[lr]::
1358::$$$message_0006_0045_0003$$$::By some trick of magecraft, there seemed no end to it.[lr]::
1359::$$$message_0006_0045_0004$$$::Its enormity made him feel all the more diminutive.[lr]::
1360::$$$message_0006_0045_0005$$$::Yes...this temple wasn't just big...[lr]::
1361::$$$message_0006_0045_0006$$$::Trembling as he ventured deeper into it, its sheer evil made him feel like an insect.::
1362::$$$message_0006_0046_0000$$$::Then...[lr]::
1363::$$$message_0006_0046_0001$$$::Minutes, no, hours later, the mirrored shield warned Perseus.[lr]::
1364::$$$message_0006_0046_0002$$$::The shield reflected information about its surroundings.[lr]::
1365::$$$message_0006_0046_0003$$$::It became a sensory device that displayed the dark temple's terrain and Perseus's heartbeat.[lr]::
1366::$$$message_0006_0046_0004$$$::...It also informed him of the approaching monster's heartbeat.::
1367::$$$message_0006_0047_0000$$$::...The scenery warped.[lr]::
1368::$$$message_0006_0047_0001$$$::Something aberrant was creeping out of the darkness.[lr]::
1369::$$$message_0006_0047_0002$$$::But he could not look directly at it.[lr]::
1370::$$$message_0006_0047_0003$$$::Perseus implored himself to never take his eyes off the shield until this quest was done.::
1371::$$$message_0006_0048_0000$$$::This battle could be avoided no longer.[lr]::
1372::$$$message_0006_0048_0001$$$::In mere seconds, he would fly into the air and challenge the monster.[lr]::
1373::$$$message_0006_0048_0002$$$::But...[lr]::
1374::$$$message_0006_0048_0003$$$::Before that, he realized something was different from the accounts.[lr]::
1375::$$$message_0006_0048_0004$$$::There were supposed to be three beautiful sisters residing in this realm.[lr]::
1376::$$$message_0006_0048_0005$$$::But the mirror was only displaying the heartbeats of himself and the monster.[lr]::
1377::$$$message_0006_0048_0006$$$::Then...[lr]::
1378::$$$message_0006_0048_0007$$$::Here was the Serpent Princess of Petrification, the monstrous Medusa...but where were the heartbeats of her sisters?::
1379::$$$message_0006_0049_0000$$$::Something enormous was trampling through the sea of stone pillars.[lr]::
1380::$$$message_0006_0049_0001$$$::This was the Gorgon monster Perseus had detected.::
1381::$$$message_0006_0050_0000$$$::Perseus cursed.[lr]::
1382::$$$message_0006_0050_0001$$$::Those damned gods. What promised glory was this?[lr]::
1383::$$$message_0006_0050_0002$$$::There was never a chance of winning this fight.[lr]::
1384::$$$message_0006_0050_0003$$$::The monster had grown too much, becoming a dark god unto itself.[lr]::
1385::$$$message_0006_0050_0004$$$::Before that, his crafty relics were little better than life preservers.::
1386::$$$message_0006_0051_0000$$$::Life preservers amidst a wrathful storm.[lr]::
1387::$$$message_0006_0051_0001$$$::Perseus was at the mercy of the raging waves, and could only hang on for dear life.[lr]::
1388::$$$message_0006_0051_0002$$$::His relics never offered him any chance of victory by overcoming his foe.[lr]::
1389::$$$message_0006_0051_0003$$$::This would be a battle of sheer endurance.[lr]::
1390::$$$message_0006_0051_0004$$$::Perhaps a genuine hero would fare better, but Perseus, who aspired to become a hero by winning this duel, had no hope of defeating the Gorgon. ::
1391::$$$message_0006_0052_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"...Perseus was still human.[font italic=false][lr]::
1392::$$$message_0006_0052_0001$$$::[font italic=true]If there was a way for him to defeat the Gorgon..."[font italic=false]::
1393::$$$message_0006_0053_0000$$$::Perseus used the winged sandals to avoid being mortally wounded.[lr]::
1394::$$$message_0006_0053_0001$$$::He avoided petrification and evaded the Gorgon's arms.[lr]::
1395::$$$message_0006_0053_0002$$$::That was all he could manage.[lr]::
1396::$$$message_0006_0053_0003$$$::The monster never saw this tribute as a threat.[lr]::
1397::$$$message_0006_0053_0004$$$::It was simply an annoying vermin.[lr]::
1398::$$$message_0006_0053_0005$$$::Finally tiring of this chase, it released the seal on its temple.::
1399::$$$message_0006_0054_0000$$$::Breaker Gorgon: Self-Seal Dark Temple[lr]::
1400::$$$message_0006_0054_0001$$$::Breaker Gorgon was a greater Bounded Field paired with the Blood Fort Andromeda that engulfs the Shapeless Isle.[lr]::
1401::$$$message_0006_0054_0002$$$::While Blood Fort Andromeda covers the world, Breaker Gorgon seals the world.[lr]::
1402::$$$message_0006_0054_0003$$$::The consciousness of someone captive in this Bounded Field would be sealed within the Gorgon, preventing them from using any abilities they possessed in the outside world.[lr]::
1403::$$$message_0006_0054_0004$$$::Unlike the Mystic Eyes, Breaker Gorgon drew in its targets merely by exposing them to the Gorgon's magical energy.[lr]::
1404::$$$message_0006_0054_0005$$$::Perseus had no means to avoid it. The monster used its power with abandon on him...::
1405::$$$message_0006_0055_0000$$$::"[font italic=true]If there was a way for him to defeat the Gorgon...[font italic=false][lr]::
1406::$$$message_0006_0055_0001$$$::[font italic=true]...it would have to be making the monster seal itself."[font italic=false]::
1407::$$$message_0006_0056_0000$$$::Kibisis.[lr]::
1408::$$$message_0006_0056_0001$$$::The sack intended to contain Medusa's head.[lr]::
1409::$$$message_0006_0056_0002$$$::For an instant, it bulged, before turning inside-out and engulfing Perseus.[lr]::
1410::$$$message_0006_0056_0003$$$::It was the concept of an inverted world. The inside of the sack became the outside, and the outside became the inside.[lr]::
1411::$$$message_0006_0056_0004$$$::In that moment, the inside was no longer within the sack, but outside of it.[lr]::
1412::$$$message_0006_0056_0005$$$::The Gorgon's Dark Temple released inward.[lr]::
1413::$$$message_0006_0056_0006$$$::This prison was turned on the Gorgon itself, who existed "outside" of the sack.::
1414::$$$message_0006_0057_0000$$$::The monster stopped moving.[lr]::
1415::$$$message_0006_0057_0001$$$::It was caught by its own Bounded Field, attacked by its own nightmares. It now suffered as [font italic=true]Medusa[font italic=false].[lr]::
1416::$$$message_0006_0057_0002$$$::No nightmare could be worse. The monster despaired, forced to confront an image of itself whose ego was still intact.[lr]::
1417::$$$message_0006_0057_0003$$$::And then...[lr]::
1418::$$$message_0006_0057_0004$$$::...came a single counterstroke.::
1419::$$$message_0006_0058_0000$$$::The immortal-slaying Harpe cleanly severed the head of the immobilized serpent princess.[lr]::
1420::$$$message_0006_0058_0001$$$::An all but invincible monster returned to being Medusa by its own doing,[lr]::
1421::$$$message_0006_0058_0002$$$::and died easily to a killing stroke, as if awakening from a dream.::
1422::$$$message_0006_0059_0000$$$::"...That's all.[lr]::
1423::$$$message_0006_0059_0001$$$::It's quite an old tale and has nothing to do with my current self, so I embellished a few details."::
1424::$$$message_0006_0060_0000$$$::Rider sips her tea.[lr]::
1425::$$$message_0006_0060_0001$$$::She's awfully calm, considering she just told me how her head got chopped off.::
1426::$$$message_0006_0061_0000$$$::"...Oh. So that's how the slaying of Medusa actually went."[lr]::
1427::$$$message_0006_0061_0001$$$::"Yes. Ever since, I've been traumatized by the sight of myself. You can see why I don't like mirrors."[lr]::
1428::$$$message_0006_0061_0002$$$::"...Yeah, makes sense. They don't literally hurt you, but they aren't good for you mentally, right?"::
1429::$$$message_0006_0062_0000$$$::"Yes.[lr]::
1430::$$$message_0006_0062_0001$$$::I should also mention that the whelp continued to wield my head as he pleased... How utterly infuriating. I say I don't like mirrors, but perhaps I should call them my sworn enemy."[lr]::
1431::$$$message_0006_0062_0002$$$::Rider mutters that she wants to break mirrors whenever she sees them.[lr]::
1432::$$$message_0006_0062_0003$$$::But...the way she referred to him...::
1433::$$$message_0006_0063_0000$$$::"By 'whelp,' you mean Perseus, right?[lr]::
1434::$$$message_0006_0063_0001$$$::From the way you told it, he...wasn't quite a victim, but it still sounds like he was taken advantage of."::
1435::$$$message_0006_0064_0000$$$::"...Yes. He was another human used by the gods. In any case, I regarded him as nothing more than a fly at the time.[lr]::
1436::$$$message_0006_0064_0001$$$::I don't exactly hate him, and could be persuaded to even feel sympathy, but..."::
1437::$$$message_0006_0065_0000$$$::"But?"[lr]::
1438::$$$message_0006_0065_0001$$$::"Personally, I just can't bring myself to like him.[lr]::
1439::$$$message_0006_0065_0002$$$::I know he became a decent person later, but I still can't."[lr]::
1440::$$$message_0006_0065_0003$$$::"Hmm... What was Perseus like?"::
1441::$$$message_0006_0066_0000$$$::"Well, if I had to describe him..."[lr]::
1442::$$$message_0006_0066_0001$$$::Rider thinks for a moment, collecting her thoughts.[lr]::
1443::$$$message_0006_0066_0002$$$::Suddenly, she looks up, as if surprised at how quickly she found the answer.::
1444::$$$message_0006_0067_0000$$$::"In a sentence, he was a successful Shinji."[lr]::
1445::$$$message_0006_0067_0001$$$::"..."[lr]::
1446::$$$message_0006_0067_0002$$$::Ahh... That paints an incredibly clear image.[lr]::
1447::$$$message_0006_0067_0003$$$::"Heavens above, I just can't stomach him.[lr]::
1448::$$$message_0006_0067_0004$$$::No point grumbling now. If only it wasn't for Kibisis..."::
1449::$$$message_0006_0068_0000$$$::Kibisis was that Bounded Field inverter that trapped Rider within her own Breaker Gorgon.[lr]::
1450::$$$message_0006_0068_0001$$$::She said that someone caught in it would have nightmares containing both joy and forbidden taboos.[lr]::
1451::$$$message_0006_0068_0002$$$::But...[lr]::
1452::$$$message_0006_0068_0003$$$::What kind of nightmare would have created a permanent trauma toward mirrors?::
1453::$$$message_0006_0069_0000$$$::"...Hey. Can I ask what you saw, Rider?"[lr]::
1454::$$$message_0006_0069_0001$$$::"..."[lr]::
1455::$$$message_0006_0069_0002$$$::"Uh, no, sorry.[lr]::
1456::$$$message_0006_0069_0003$$$::You wouldn't want to remember or talk about your own nightmares. I'm sorry I asked."::
1457::$$$message_0006_0070_0000$$$::"...No.[lr]::
1458::$$$message_0006_0070_0001$$$::We both dream. It wouldn't be fair to you if I didn't explain."[lr]::
1459::$$$message_0006_0070_0002$$$::Rider sits up straight again.[lr]::
1460::$$$message_0006_0070_0003$$$::That said, she's still slouching a little.[lr]::
1461::$$$message_0006_0070_0004$$$::...Hrm. It seems like she finds this more palatable than the story about getting her head cut off.[lr]::
1462::$$$message_0006_0070_0005$$$::"My nightmare was..."::
1463::$$$message_0006_0071_0000$$$::[hfu]"[hfl]"[hfu]Me[hfl]Me[hfu]d[hfl]d[hfu]uu[hfl]uu[hfu]us[hfl]us[hfu]aa. [hfl]aa. [hfu]C[hfl]C[hfu]o[hfl]o[hfu]me [hfl]me [hfu]o[hfl]o[hfu]o[hfl]oo[hfu]o[hfl]u[hfu]uu[hfl]uu[hfu]t, [hfl]t, [hfu]Me[hfl]Me[hfu]d[hfl]d[hfu]u[hfl]u[hfu]u[hfl]u[hfu]saa[hfl]saa[hfu]..."[hfl]..."::
1464::$$$message_0006_0072_0000$$$::"...Y-yes? I'm here.[lr]::
1465::$$$message_0006_0072_0001$$$::What is it, Big Sister, Middle Sister?"::
1466::$$$message_0006_0072_0002$$$::"Don't give us that.[lr]::
1467::$$$message_0006_0072_0003$$$::You know that I and myself are due to attend Lord Poseidon's banquet tonight."::
1468::$$$message_0006_0072_0004$$$::"...Haah. I did hear that the sea god summoned you. But...what about it?"::
1469::$$$message_0006_0072_0005$$$::"Rrgh...! Hey, did you hear that, me!?[lr]::
1470::$$$message_0006_0072_0006$$$::How is our giant little sister this useless!?"::
1471::$$$message_0006_0072_0007$$$::"She really is such a troublesome, insensitive girl."::
1472::$$$message_0006_0072_0008$$$::"Medusa, are you perhaps a dinosaur?[lr]::
1473::$$$message_0006_0072_0009$$$::Is your brain even smaller than the palms of our hands?"::
1474::$$$message_0006_0072_0010$$$::"...U-um, Sisters?[lr]::
1475::$$$message_0006_0072_0011$$$::If you, er, need help getting ready for dinner, I can help you..."::
1476::$$$message_0006_0072_0012$$$::"Ugh, you're so annoying![lr]::
1477::$$$message_0006_0072_0013$$$::I'm asking if our dresses are ready yet!"::
1478::$$$message_0006_0073_0000$$$::"Eh... Uh, yes! I'll get them ready!"::
1479::$$$message_0006_0073_0001$$$::"You'll [font italic=true]get[font italic=false] them ready? You mean it's not done yet?"::
1480::$$$message_0006_0073_0002$$$::"I'm sure she's dragging her feet because she likes embarrassing us."::
1481::$$$message_0006_0074_0000$$$::"I would never do such a thing![hfchance layer=1][lr]::
1482::$$$message_0006_0074_0001$$$::I-I...!"::
1483::$$$message_0006_0074_0002$$$::"What's that? [hffeelgood layer=0] Hey, me. Is it just me, or does she seem uppity? She really is ugly for a lady."::
1484::$$$message_0006_0074_0003$$$::"Yes. I pity her, but we should rake her over the coals a bit."::
1485::$$$message_0006_0074_0004$$$::"It's all for our adorable little sister. It might seem a little excessive, but this is the time to steel ourselves and correct her flaws."::
1486::$$$message_0006_0074_0005$$$::"Ah, eek...![lr]::
1487::$$$message_0006_0074_0006$$$::B-Big Sister, [hfwww layer=1]I'm sorry! I regret my actions...!"::
1488::$$$message_0006_0075_0000$$$::"I'll do my best starting tomorrow, so please forgive me todayyyy!"::
1489::$$$message_0006_0075_0001$$$::"...Hehe. That's right, shrink down and become small like that."::
1490::$$$message_0006_0076_0000$$$::"All right, a fun feast is about to start, so we'll forgive you today. Now Medusa, about our dresses..."::
1491::$$$message_0006_0076_0001$$$::"Ah... W-what, Middle Sister?"::
1492::$$$message_0006_0076_0002$$$::"What were you thinking!?[lr]::
1493::$$$message_0006_0076_0003$$$::Unbelievable. Why are there three dresses for us!?"::
1494::$$$message_0006_0076_0004$$$::"Eh...ehehe.[lr]::
1495::$$$message_0006_0076_0005$$$::Um, I kept this a secret, but he actually invited me too[line len=2]"::
1496::$$$message_0006_0076_0006$$$::"Impossible![lr]::
1497::$$$message_0006_0076_0007$$$::[large]Hm[rf]ph, how do you like this!?"[wvs][se storage=se673.wav]::
1498::$$$message_0006_0077_0000$$$::"Heeeeyaaaagh!?"::
1499::$$$message_0006_0077_0001$$$::"S-S-Sister, I just made that dress! Why are you handling it like you're scaling a fish!?"::
1500::$$$message_0006_0077_0002$$$::"Hehehe. I sure am merciless."::
1501::$$$message_0006_0077_0003$$$::"Tragically, it looks like you won't be attending the feast tonight, Medusa."::
1502::$$$message_0006_0077_0004$$$::"Ah, ah, ah... You're so mean, Middle Sister... Why would you do such a thing!?"::
1503::$$$message_0006_0077_0005$$$::"Hmph. It's a millennia too early for you."::
1504::$$$message_0006_0077_0006$$$::"Listen, Medusa. Are you really arrogant enough to think someone of your standing can come to the party?"::
1505::$$$message_0006_0077_0007$$$::"That's something you only get to do once there is a fan club for big folks."::
1506::$$$message_0006_0077_0008$$$::"My, you're being so harsh, me.[lr]::
1507::$$$message_0006_0077_0009$$$::If that's the case, Medusa will never be able to debut in high society."::
1508::$$$message_0006_0077_0010$$$::"Big Sister, what do you mean..."::
1509::$$$message_0006_0077_0011$$$::"Don't you get what I'm saying?[lr]::
1510::$$$message_0006_0077_0012$$$::Nobody likes big women like you!"::
1511::$$$message_0006_0078_0000$$$::"In fact, we wouldn't tolerate it even if someone did.[lr]::
1512::$$$message_0006_0078_0001$$$::As if there's any man [hfchance layer=1]who would be a good fit for you!"::
1513::$$$message_0006_0078_0002$$$::"That's right. Unfortunately, the men who would look at you are few and far between."::
1514::$$$message_0006_0078_0003$$$::"Think of how unromantic the kisses would be.[lr]::
1515::$$$message_0006_0078_0004$$$::If a man has to stand on tiptoe to kiss a woman, that's a death sentence for romance."::
1516::$$$message_0006_0078_0005$$$::"Th-that's... I'm not tall because I want to be..."::
1517::$$$message_0006_0078_0006$$$::"...And I don't actually think I'm that tall..."::
1518::$$$message_0006_0078_0007$$$::"Ahahaha! You say that even though you try your best to look smaller!? If you don't like what we're saying, then get on our level!"::
1519::$$$message_0006_0078_0008$$$::"We're small and beautiful enough to be swept off our feet, but it would take someone as mighty as Atlas to pick you up."::
1520::$$$message_0006_0078_0009$$$::"Yes. I'm sure he'd still develop back pain, though."::
1521::$$$message_0006_0078_0010$$$::"Get it? The trend right now is slim and compact. [hfchance layer=0]No one wants a big woman like you who's built like a farm horse."::
1522::$$$message_0006_0078_0011$$$::"Ah, uuu... You didn't have to say it like that."::
1523::$$$message_0006_0078_0012$$$::"Hehe. Tears won't save you.[lr]::
1524::$$$message_0006_0078_0013$$$::If you start crying, the man will think there's a leak in the ceiling."::
1525::$$$message_0006_0078_0014$$$::"Oh my, now I feel bad for her, hearing other me say that.[lr]::
1526::$$$message_0006_0078_0015$$$::Did you know that I've seen Medusa sighing in the mirror?"::
1527::$$$message_0006_0078_0016$$$::"Don't you think it's positively wretched?"::
1528::$$$message_0006_0079_0000$$$::"That's why I've been considering asking Lord Poseidon to give us his concave mirror."::
1529::$$$message_0006_0079_0001$$$::"Pft. Because it would make her look smaller and cuter?"::
1530::$$$message_0006_0080_0000$$$::"Ahaha, great idea! Let's ask Lord Poseidon to make us a really big mirror!"::
1531::$$$message_0006_0081_0000$$$::"Of course, this is what we'll tell him when he asks why[line len=2]"::
1532::$$$message_0006_0082_0000$$$::"'To our great shame, our younger sister has a mental illness that prevents her from looking directly at flat mirrors.'"::
1533::$$$message_0006_0082_0001$$$::"How wonderful.[lr]::
1534::$$$message_0006_0082_0002$$$::Oh, we're such thoughtful big sisters, aren't we, Medusa?"[playstop time=3500 nowait=1]::
1535::$$$message_0006_0082_0003$$$::"Uuuu, Sisters... Waaaaaaah!"::
1536::$$$message_0006_0083_0000$$$::And so...[lr]::
1537::$$$message_0006_0083_0001$$$::Rider's had her eyes closed for a few minutes after looking like she was about to say something.::
1538::$$$message_0006_0084_0000$$$::"...Um, Rider?[lr]::
1539::$$$message_0006_0084_0001$$$::You were going to tell me your nightmare."[lr]::
1540::$$$message_0006_0084_0002$$$::"...I changed my mind. Let's stop talking about these old stories.[lr]::
1541::$$$message_0006_0084_0003$$$::It's also almost time for my appointment."::
1542::$$$message_0006_0085_0000$$$::Rider stands up.[lr]::
1543::$$$message_0006_0085_0001$$$::I feel guilty. It really was insensitive of me to ask.::
1544::$$$message_0006_0086_0000$$$::"I'm heading out.[lr]::
1545::$$$message_0006_0086_0001$$$::...Just so you don't misunderstand, the nightmare Kibisis showed me wasn't actually that horrible.[lr]::
1546::$$$message_0006_0086_0002$$$::It wasn't pain that put a stop to me...but the joy of reuniting with people I thought I'd never see again."::
1547::$$$message_0006_0087_0000$$$::"Huh...?"[lr]::
1548::$$$message_0006_0087_0001$$$::"It was like your life now, Shirou.[lr]::
1549::$$$message_0006_0087_0002$$$::They pushed me around all the time, but those were the best days of my life. ...Perhaps the reason I dislike mirrors is because they remind me of those memories."::
1550::$$$message_0006_0088_0000$$$::Rider smiles kindly and leaves.[lr]::
1551::$$$message_0006_0088_0001$$$::"...Hm."[lr]::
1552::$$$message_0006_0088_0002$$$::That smile of hers is infectious.[lr]::
1553::$$$message_0006_0088_0003$$$::It makes me happy, but...::
1554::$$$message_0006_0089_0000$$$::"I'm not being pushed around all the time, Rider."[lr]::
1555::$$$message_0006_0089_0001$$$::Really, I'm not.[lr]::
1556::$$$message_0006_0089_0002$$$::What's this sudden feeling of kinship toward her?::
901535::$$$message_9006_0082_0003$$$::"Uuuu, Sisters... Waaaaaaah!"[r]::

